{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q425446","formula":"C₁₉H₄₀","hill":"C19H40","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":40.0},"names":{"en":"Pristane","ru":"Пристан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Pristane is a natural saturated terpenoid alkane obtained primarily from shark liver oil, from which its name is derived (Latin pristis, \"shark\"). It is also found in the stomach oil of birds in the order Procellariiformes and in mineral oil and some foods. Pristane and phytane are used in the fields of geology and environmental science as biomarkers to characterize origins and evolution of petroleum hydrocarbons and coal.","ru":"Приста́н (2,6,10,14-тетраметилпентадекан) — природный насыщенный терпеноидный алкан, получаемый прежде всего из жира печени акул, от которых и произошло его название (лат. pristis — «акула»); один из структурных изомеров нонадекана. Пристан также обнаружен в минеральном масле и желудочном масле птиц."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":15979,"mass":268.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)CCCC(C)CCCC(C)CCCC(C)C","inchikey":"XOJVVFBFDXDTEG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,6,10,14-tetramethylpentadecane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"15979","atoms":59,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.77,"y":1.86,"z":-1.057,"el":"C"},{"x":1.184,"y":2.136,"z":1.326,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.601,"y":2.408,"z":-0.205,"el":"C"},{"x":0.926,"y":2.825,"z":-0.034,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.23,"y":2.269,"z":-0.877,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.561,"y":0.375,"z":-1.423,"el":"C"},{"x":1.362,"y":0.611,"z":1.169,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.542,"y":-0.619,"z":-0.253,"el":"C"},{"x":2.525,"y":0.151,"z":0.279,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.404,"y":-2.079,"z":-0.697,"el":"C"},{"x":2.597,"y":-1.37,"z":0.112,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.082,"y":2.077,"z":-0.294,"el":"C"},{"x":2.406,"y":2.787,"z":1.985,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.401,"y":-3.078,"z":0.477,"el":"C"},{"x":